# [EN] Normalize line endings on checkout regardless of a contributor's local `core.autocrlf`, so text files (shell
#      scripts, source, docs, metadata such as `UPSTREAM_COMMIT`) are always LF. Without this file, a Windows checkout
#      with `core.autocrlf=true` silently rewrites tracked text files to CRLF, which breaks `scripts/*.sh` (the
#      shebang line) and the strict `^commit=[0-9a-f]{40}$` check in `scripts/check_package_licenses.py` (see
#      `docs/Task-Log.md`, "git cz style, English only" session's fix, 2026-11-20). Binary assets are listed
#      explicitly so Git's content-sniffing heuristic never mis-normalizes them.
# [CN] 无论贡献者本地 `core.autocrlf` 如何设置，检出时统一换行符，使文本文件（shell 脚本、源码、文档、`UPSTREAM_COMMIT` 等元数据文件）始终为
#      LF。没有本文件时，Windows 上 `core.autocrlf=true` 的检出会把已跟踪的文本文件悄悄改为 CRLF，既会破坏 `scripts/*.sh` 的 shebang 行，
#      也会让 `scripts/check_package_licenses.py` 中 `^commit=[0-9a-f]{40}$` 的严格匹配失败。下面显式列出二进制资源，避免 Git
#      的内容嗅探启发式误判。

* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh text eol=lf

# [EN] Binary assets: never normalized, never diffed as text.
# [CN] 二进制资源：不做换行符归一化，也不按文本做 diff。
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.riv binary
*.pag binary
*.svga binary
*.bin binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.car binary
*.zip binary
*.icns binary
